# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PRIVACY GUARD — do not remove.
#
# This repository starts PRIVATE, and becomes PUBLIC when the site is
# published (free GitHub Pages on an organization requires a public repo).
# Treat it as public from day one.
# GSSA Bylaws Art. IX 9.3 restricts records containing private student
# information to those with a legitimate organizational need.
#
# The membership roster, meeting minutes, officer applications, budgets and
# scoring rubrics must NEVER be committed here. They live in the officers'
# SLU Google Workspace, owned by the Secretary and VP of Finance.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
docs/
../docs/
*.docx
*.xlsx
*.xlsm
*.pdf
roster*
members*
applications*

# ...but the governing documents are meant to be published. The blanket *.pdf
# rule above would otherwise silently drop the bylaws and the Bylaws section
# on the home page would fall back to its "not uploaded yet" placeholder.
!src/media/*.pdf

# Full-size originals kept on disk for re-editing. The site serves the resized
# copies; committing a 4-5 MB source would sit in git history permanently.
src/assets/img/slu_campus_2.jpg

# Build output
_site/

# Dependencies
node_modules/

# Environment / editor
.env
.env.*
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/
*.log
npm-debug.log*
.eleventy-cache/
